{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Unto Moses and unto Aaron</b> — Because \"by the mouth of the priest shall every controversy and every plague be\" (Deuteronomy 21:5), the speech was also to Aaron — or to Moses, that he should tell Aaron, according to our Rabbis (Mekhilta, beginning). And it does not say here \"Speak unto the children of Israel,\" because the priests, when they see the unclean, will compel them to be shut up and to be purified. And in the section of purification (below, 14:1–2) it says \"unto Moses, saying: This shall be the law of the metzora,\" for there is no need to warn Israel concerning purification, nor the priest concerning the offering of the sacrifices, for they will do so willingly. And in the section of the zav it says (ibid. 15:2) \"Speak unto the children of Israel and say unto them,\" because it is a hidden matter and no one recognizes it; He warns them that each person must inform the priest of his condition."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:53:13.269769540Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}